---
import Section from '../Section.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    id: 'faq-1',
    question: 'What kinds of operational problems does Guava work on?',
    paragraphs: [
      'Guava works on operational problems where the current way of working is manual, slow, unreliable, or spread across disconnected systems and individual knowledge.',
      'Typical starting points include disconnected systems, high volumes of manual data handling, slow or inaccurate reporting, unreliable inventory signals, and processes that stall on exceptions or handoffs.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'faq-2',
    question: 'Can Guava work with our existing software and systems?',
    paragraphs: [
      'Yes. Replacing existing systems is not the default. Guava can work across existing software, databases, spreadsheets, APIs, reporting systems, and internal workflows.',
      'The objective is to select the simplest intervention that produces the required outcome.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'faq-3',
    question: 'How do you decide what should be automated?',
    paragraphs: [
      'The workflow should have a meaningful business consequence and enough repeatability or operational burden to justify intervention. We evaluate the process, systems, data, exceptions, risks, and expected outcome before deciding what should be automated.',
      'Some problems require software. Some require process changes. Some should not be automated at all.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'faq-4',
    question: 'What happens when we first talk?',
    paragraphs: [
      'We start with your operating problem, not with a technology. A first conversation is a focused discussion of how the work currently gets done, where it breaks or slows down, and what the outcome needs to be.',
      'From there we explain how Guava would approach it, what a practical path forward looks like, and whether a focused paid Diagnostic is useful before scoping the build.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<Section variant="white" id="faq" container="narrow" label="FAQ">
  <h2 class="text-h2 mb-md">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <p class="text-muted mb-lg">
    Questions focused on operational technology, automation, systems, and
    getting started.
  </p>

  <div class="divide-y divide-text/10 border-y border-text/10">
    {faqs.map((faq) => (
      <div class="py-md" data-faq-item>
        <button
          type="button"
          id={`${faq.id}-button`}
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls={`${faq.id}-panel`}
          class="flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-md rounded-sm py-xs text-left text-body font-semibold text-text transition-colors duration-fast hover:text-brand focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand"
        >
          <span>{faq.question}</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0 text-lg text-brand">+</span>
        </button>
        <div id={`${faq.id}-panel`} role="region" aria-labelledby={`${faq.id}-button`} hidden>
          <div class="pt-sm">
            {faq.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => (
              <p class="text-body text-muted mb-sm">{paragraph}</p>
            ))}
            {faq.list && (
              <ul class="list-disc pl-md mb-sm space-y-xs">
                {faq.list.map((item) => (
                  <li class="text-body text-muted">{item}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            )}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</Section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-faq-item]').forEach((item) => {
    const button = item.querySelector('button[aria-expanded]');
    const panel = item.querySelector('[role="region"]');
    const indicator = button.querySelector('[aria-hidden="true"]');

    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const expanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
      panel.hidden = expanded;
      indicator.textContent = expanded ? '+' : '\u2212';
    });
  });
</script>